{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"5c86613a636ddafb6c78434a46cce1f1ddda8051a8960dc4527a703dda5d6a02","packTokens":2496,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1094,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":841,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using their Folio3 Google account, with employee profiles and vehicle details populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking with a single action and view its status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can schedule or cancel parking releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can view availability and claim released parking on a first-come, first-served basis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and generate and email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What may Parking Administrators and Security Guards do in the web app, beyond the functions already described?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Administrators manage employee and parking records, assignments, configuration, and report recipients; guards use only the entrance indicator and existing sticker process.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may receive reports that identify employees and their unused parking, and how are recipients maintained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Parking Administrator maintains a named recipient list; only those recipients receive the report.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which source is authoritative for employee profiles, dedicated-parking assignments, and registered vehicles when an employee signs in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the corporate directory for employee details and an administrator-maintained parking assignment and vehicle list.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"For an employee with multiple registered vehicles, what counts as parking utilization when any one of their plates is detected entering that day?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Count the allocation as used if any vehicle registered to that employee is detected.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How long should parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events be retained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply Folio3's existing records-retention policy to these records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"What makes an employee without dedicated parking eligible to claim a released space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any active Folio3 employee without a dedicated assignment who has at least one registered vehicle may claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Can a temporary parking user cancel a claim after successfully claiming a space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Claims cannot be cancelled by the user once confirmed.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"If a dedicated holder's released space has been claimed but the holder's permanently stickered vehicle arrives, how should the system treat the temporary claimant's authorization?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the temporary authorization valid; the stickered vehicle continues through the existing process even if this exceeds configured capacity.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 24 requirements proceed as one implementation run, or should scope be reduced for this run?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 24 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How must an LPR verification request prove it comes from trusted Folio3 equipment before it can activate the entrance indicator?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require the request to be authenticated as coming from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may view employee utilization records and export them as CSV?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only Parking Administrators may view and export utilization records; deny access to all other roles.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"What should deployment do if no designated active Folio3 bootstrap account is supplied?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not complete administrator setup until deployment configuration supplies a designated active Folio3 account; grant that account the initial Parking Administrator role.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"When verification fails while the green indicator may already be active, what should the system do with the indicator?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Explicitly set the green indicator inactive on every verification failure.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build the Folio3 Parking product as a responsive web app for phone, tablet, and desktop, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Authenticate only active Folio3 employees through corporate Google Workspace, and provide their profiles with directory details and administrator-maintained parking assignments and vehicle records; require employees to register a license plate before release or claim operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Give Parking Administrators read-only access to directory details and the ability to create, view, and update employee parking assignments and vehicle records, configure release times, floor capacities, work calendars, report recipients and role assignments, and manage initial administrator setup through deployment bootstrap configuration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Let dedicated parking holders release parking once for the current date or schedule releases up to 30 days ahead, make eligible releases claimable at the configured daily release time, show reservation and release status, and permit cancellation only before a release is claimed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Show claimable parking and current available-space counts to active employees who have no dedicated assignment and at least one registered vehicle; assign each release to only the earliest accepted eligible claim, include the assigned floor, and prevent claimants from cancelling confirmed temporary claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Send eligible employees an email using a fixed template when a released allocation becomes claimable, and preserve existing permanent sticker processes and any temporary claim already made for that date, even when capacity is exceeded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Authenticate entrance-verification requests from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment, verify readable plates against current-date temporary authorizations, activate the green indicator only for valid authorizations, explicitly set it inactive when verification fails, and record verification attempts and integration errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Record daily utilization using registered-vehicle entry records, counting an allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected, and generate Monday-morning weekly reports with unused parking, utilization statistics, release and claim totals, and the specified utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Send weekly report emails only to configured named recipients, and provide filterable on-screen utilization lists and CSV export exclusively to Parking Administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Retain parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events according to Folio3's records-retention policy, and limit Phase 1 utilization functionality to monitoring, recording, and reporting without automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}